It's not as varied or as modern as Naughty Dog's 'Last of us', but the audio, graphics, story , gameplay and complexity of Rockstar Games L.A. Noire is still one of the best for this genre and I've no idea why David Cage after all these years, still hasn't learned how to make a decent and believable game []o_O]
Despite being a poorly ported to Steam for Windows OS and being over two years old, it still sounds and looks far better than any current XB1 or PS4 ...thing. The games atmosphere drips film noire with authenticity to match and some brilliant acting/voice overs, which all make it truly feel like L.A. Confidential the video game {}^_^}
Naughty Dog (much like Psygnosis was) is pretty much Sony's ♥♥♥♥♥ now, so we won't be getting of there fine work (though limited to 720p/30fps), so for us Steam for Windows OS only users, L.A. Noire is outstanding and highly recommend alternative []^_^]

Dont get me wrong, i love this game, but what they did with their last patch or two made it unplayable for people with a bit lower specs (even for some good machines) . I paid for it thinking it really deserved the money, and only a couple minutes after it proved me wrong. It is so unoptimazed at the moment that even with the lowest settings and altered ini files i cant get it to run smoothly. It aint even a framerate problem cause i get around 50,60 fps which should be enough to play or at least enough to prevent picture tearing. There is a video on youtube (
) that shows what i m talking about. Its really frustrating and i would advise anyone to reconsider buying this until the problem is resolved. Anyway this is an amazing game and that makes it even harder to deal with its bugs.
So this in a way is a plead to TB to fix this asap.

The first time you get into this game, you are, usually, either lost either undecided.
Undecided of what to do, what to see, what to click... Click click click...
When this doesn't happen, you click.
In this game, you click for loads of things :
- To get your power-ups ;
- To be a clicker ;
- To be a hero ;
- To chat with your group ;
- To make sure the game didn't freeze (usually after you went away, even thought the game continues to play without you ;
- Sort of good graphics, uncommon, in my opinion ;
- Easy understanding of the game (they is no tutorial so that's needed) ;
- AFK help (the game sort of still runs without you) ;
- Fast-clicks and clicks.
- The clan search system ;
- Not mind breaking ; mouse breaking, though.
9/10 : this game made me break my mouse, twice.
Hum...

