I'll keep it short and quick.
The good;
Great graphics, many things to create, huge worlds to explore,Difficult enemies to fight, and many secrets to find
The bad;
Awful hit boxes, losing everything and having a hard time getting it back with no option to turn that off, the entire unreal engine and all of its unoptimized glory, again... The unreal engine's mod system is A joke, and all the time you will waste grinding away weeks, months, or years of your life trying to build something only for it to be destroyed including all your weapons and difficult to make armor that is gone in the blink of an eye with no way to repair it on the go.
I do understand that this is a survival game and I did have fun playing it for a short time. After a while, the magic wears off and the insurmountable grinding just becomes repetitive and kills the fun that you are having.

It's good for two things;
1: Time Wasting
2: Running while you do other stuff
